 34AL cG E$from 2013StZY.                                                       
 34AL cG $2023Lu07 observed the 803|g within the 100-ms window following the    
 34AL2cG arrival of a {+36}Mg ion in both NSCL and FRIB experiments.            
 34AL cG $2013StZY observed a 804-keV |g ray that was not in coincidence with   
 34AL2cG other |g rays. 2013StZY states that the 804|g is a prompt line that    
 34AL3cG predominantly appears in the time window 0-10 ms after an implantation 
 34AL4cG of {+36}Mg, so it must originate from a deexcitation in one of the     
 34AL5cG daughter nuclei {+34,34,36}Al.                                         

